''Tos'' has a particle variant, τι, του, ''-t, -τ''. The particles τι and του, used after a demonstrative pronoun, or suffixed to it as ''-t'' or -τ, seem to emphasize the following noun: σεμουν του κνουμανει ("to this very tomb").

Another anaphoric pronoun is ''oy''&nbsp;/ ''ioi''. It only occurs as a dative singular, ''oy'', ιοι, οι ("to him, to her").<ref>Obrador Cursach (2018), pp. 80, 207.</ref>

The [[intensive pronoun|emphatic pronoun]] ''autos'' ("the very one, the same"; cf. Greek αὐτός) can also be used anaphorically. Its composite ''ve(n)autos'' is a [[reflexive pronoun]], meaning "himself" (Greek ἑαυτός).<ref>Obrador Cursach (2018), pp. 81, 150–151, 192.</ref>

